18	// always minutes behind and every session it reaches is overdue; an overdue session used to be claimed at
19	// any hour, which put the whole population online through its own night. A login keeps the hour it was
20	// scheduled for: the one the routine placed in the dark period -- the wake the account takes for an attack
21	// landing then -- is still taken then, and a login it owed its day waits for its next waking day.
