 15	/**
 16	 * Drive a named situation on the cohort this container points at, in seconds.
 17	 *
 18	 * The harness could not test behaviour that needs time to pass: a hostile fleet takes hours to
 19	 * arrive, a queue order takes hours to finish, a session only fires when the scheduler says so, and
 20	 * the whole loop parks for a peak window. So nothing that depends on a situation -- a fleet save, a
 21	 * recycle, a raid -- could be exercised except by waiting.
 22	 *
 23	 * This makes the time pass instead of waiting for it: it rewrites the rows the real clock is compared
 24	 * against (host queues, the module's due work and schedules), runs the host's own apply step, and
 25	 * drives `ai:run-due-work` with a synchronous queue so the sessions run in this process rather than in
 26	 * a Horizon worker some seconds later. Then it reads back what the account did and exits non-zero when
 27	 * the answer is missing.
 28	 *
 29	 *   php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php list
 30	 *   php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php run idle-planet
 31	 *   php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php run inbound-attack --confirm --accounts=2
 32	 *   php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php run all --confirm --wait=300
 33	 *
 34	 * `--arrival` must sit inside the account's own reaction lead (provoke-ai.php prints it:
 35	 * 120 + 60 x session interval), or "it did not save" is the account correctly waiting for a fleet
 36	 * that is still seven minutes out rather than a defect.
 37	 *
 38	 * Peak windows: no provider call is made anywhere in this file, so this is work to run *inside* a peak
 39	 * window -- it is what the loop can do while it waits out the window instead of sleeping.
 40	 *
 41	 * DEV TOOLING, never shipped behaviour. The scenarios that write to the world (a hostile fleet, a
 42	 * debris field, loot beside a planet) refuse to run without --confirm: on grand and pve those writes
 43	 * are real, which is the point, but not something that should happen because a script was typed with
 44	 * the wrong universe in front of it. The database the container points at decides the cohort.
 45	 */
