    /**
     * Whether the account's own clock has come for this item.
     *
     * An accelerated session is claimable the moment its account is awake (that is what shortens the
     * waits), and any item is claimable once its own due time has passed. A session is the exception:
     * the one a session leaves behind is due seconds later, so a worker that is minutes behind finds
     * every session in the cohort overdue, and an overdue session used to be claimable at any hour --
     * which put the whole population online through its own night (AUTH_UPTIME). A session therefore
     * waits for its account's waking window, whatever hour it was moved to.
     */
    private function dueForAccount(AiWorkItem $workItem): bool
    {
        if ($workItem->due_at->isFuture()) {
            return $this->acceleratedSession($workItem);
        }

        return $workItem->kind !== AiWorkKind::RunSession || $this->sessionFallsInTheWakingWindow($workItem);
    }

    /**
     * A login happens inside the account's own waking window; the night is spent asleep.
     *
     * The routine places every successor inside the window -- both the reaction wake to an inbound and the
     * material-event wake are deferred when they would land in the account's night -- so a login that comes
     * due in the dark period was moved there by something else: a worker's backlog, a retry, a maintenance
     * pass or an operator driving the account. Taking it then would put the account online at an hour it
     * sleeps, which is exactly what the host's round-the-clock signal counts (AUTH_UPTIME): an account whose
     * logins cover eighteen hours of the day is not a player, and eight whole hours of every day have to stay
     * silent. The login waits and is taken when the account wakes.
     */
    private function sessionFallsInTheWakingWindow(AiWorkItem $workItem): bool
    {
        $profile = $this->workProfile($workItem);

        return $profile === null || app(SessionPlanner::class)->isAwake($profile, now()->toImmutable());
    }
